message.content:
Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows how to create a “flip‑card” that rotates when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Hover‑Rotate Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    font-family:sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card container ---------- */
.card {
    width:260px;
    height:160px;
    perspective:800px;          /* Gives a 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Inner wrapper that will be rotated ---------- */
.card-inner {
    position:relative;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    transition:transform 0.6s;
    transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3D children */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Front & back faces ---------- */
.card-front,
.card-back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* Hide the back face when turned */
    border-radius:12px;
    box-shadow:0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    font-size:1.4rem;
    color:white;
}

.card-front { background:#3498db; }
.card-back  { background:#e74c3c; transform:rotateY(180deg); }

/* ---------- 5️⃣  Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <div class="card-front">Front Side</div>
        <div class="card-back">Back Side</div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | `perspective` on `.card` | Creates a 3‑D space so the rotation looks realistic. |
| 2 | `.card-inner` has `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps child elements (front/back) in 3‑D. |
| 3 | `backface-visibility:hidden` | Hides the backside of each face when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| 4 | On hover, `.card-inner` rotates 180° around the Y‑axis | Flips the card to show the other side. |

You can replace the text, colors, or add more styling (shadows, gradients, etc.) to match your design. Happy coding!
